@startuml C4-Dynamic-ZeroTrust-Target
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

title Dynamic — Zero Trust target (IAM as PDP, resource servers as PEPs)

autonumber
actor "End User" as user
actor "IAM Administrator" as admin
participant "Client\niOS (DPoP) / Web BFF" as client <<ui>>
participant "Explore AI API\nPEP" as ai <<java>>
participant "Explore IAM\nPDP :9100" as iam <<java>>
participant "Key Management\nKMS" as kms <<external>>
participant "Explore ML\nPEP (private network)" as ml <<python>>
participant "Audit Sink / SIEM" as siem <<external>>

== Sign in (Phase 0 aud · Phase 1 MFA, rotation · Phase 3 per-user scope, DPoP) ==
user -> client: Sign in
client -> iam: /oauth2/authorize\nPKCE S256 + resource=explore-ai
iam -> user: WebAuthn / Passkey (MFA)
iam -> iam: Grant only the user's scopes\n(users / groups / roles)
client -> iam: POST /oauth2/token + DPoP proof
iam -> kms: Sign with current key
iam --> client: Access Token 5–15 min\naud=explore-ai, cnf=DPoP key\n+ rotating Refresh Token
iam -> siem: Token issued (traceparent)

== Request at the PEP (Phase 0) ==
client -> ai: Bearer + DPoP proof + traceparent
ai -> iam: JWKS (cached, current + next key)
ai -> ai: Verify iss, signature, exp,\naud=explore-ai, scope, DPoP

== High-risk operation (Phase 3) ==
ai -> iam: Evaluate(principal, action, resource,\nconditions: MFA freshness, device)
iam -> iam: PolicyEngine:\nexplicit Deny > Allow > implicit Deny
alt Deny or step-up required
  iam --> ai: Deny / step-up
  ai --> client: 403 or re-authenticate
else Allow
  iam --> ai: Allow + ReasonCode
end

== Call downstream on behalf of the user (Phase 2) ==
ai -> iam: Token Exchange (RFC 8693)\nsubject_token=user token, audience=explore-ml\n(client_credentials service identity)
iam --> ai: Downstream token\naud=explore-ml, sub=user, act=explore-ai,\nscope narrowed
ai -> ml: Downstream token + traceparent (TLS / mTLS)
ml -> ml: Verify iss, signature, exp,\naud=explore-ml, scope
ml --> ai: Result
ai --> client: 200
ai -> siem: Access log (traceparent)
ml -> siem: Access log (traceparent)

== Continuous verification and revocation (Phase 1 · Phase 4) ==
alt Administrator disables the user
  admin -> iam: POST /api/v1/users/{user}:disable
else Refresh token reuse detected
  client -> iam: Reused Refresh Token
end
iam -> iam: Revoke session, token family,\nSTS sessions
iam -> siem: Revocation event (traceparent)
client -> iam: Next refresh
iam --> client: invalid_grant → sign in again

note over ai, ml
  Explore Chat follows the same PEP path
  (aud=explore-chat; Socket.IO origin allow-list).
  Status and gaps: Zero-Trust-Architecture.md
end note

@enduml
